  "summary": "The house-ball community of Black and Latino LGBTQ+ performers: category walks, vogue, realness and chosen families.",
  "description": "From Harlem's 1960s-80s balls (Paris is Burning documents the 80s peak) grew the house-ball scene: chosen \"houses\", categories from face to realness to vogue — the angular, Egyptian-figured dance inspired by Vogue poses. Ballroom fashion spans realness categories, gender performance and legendary couture-level homemade looks. Madonna's \"Vogue\" (1990) mainstreamed the dance; today global ballroom scenes and Legends documentaries carry the culture while crediting its founders.",
